+## Browser port: exact implementation and acceptance steps
+
+This is a port specification; no browser implementation or browser speed claim is included in this experiment.
+
+1. **Freeze the artifact.** Merge `arith-s1r2/adapter_step500` into `Qwen/Qwen3-4B` using
+   `scan_forward.load_merged` / `pb_eval.merge_adapter`. Export those merged weights, configuration and tokenizer
+   to a browser GPU backend that exposes explicit per-layer past K/V, position IDs and attention masks. Record
+   file hashes, precision/quantization, backend version and GPU identity. A backend that only offers a chat or
+   generation API is insufficient. The current bf16 model needs a substantial device-memory budget; any smaller
+   quantized export is a new model configuration and must pass its own certificate.
+2. **Export the machine, not natural-language prompts.** Serialize `stack_machine.row_records` in its sorted
+   order and `stack_forward.machine_spec` with assignment 0: role→token IDs, newline ID, Π, start state, BOT,
+   halting states and each row's stack operation. Use the saved `cert.json` IDs to check the export. Each Π row
+   is exactly `[top, q, a, q2, newline]`; P is 250/720/1,470 for Dyck-2/Dyck-4/Boolean. No chat template, BOS,
+   padding or tokenizer-added special tokens may enter these integer sequences.
+3. **Port the trusted host machine.** Use an array of integer frame symbols initialized to BOT and one control
+   state. Translate `apply` operations `stay`, `rewrite`, `push`, `pop`, `store_push`; prohibit popping BOT.
+   Preserve child-result transfer in `bool_delta`. Port the closed-cover check and reference tests before GPU
+   inference. For infix Boolean text, use an iterative parser with `not > and > or` precedence, accepting only
+   Boolean literals/operators/parentheses, then emit the same prefix tokens and final END. Reject unknown tokens
+   explicitly. Validate the parser on all 250 pinned BBH inputs and the random-expression tests.
+4. **Prefill once.** Run Π at positions 0…P−1 with a causal mask; retain its per-layer K/V as immutable buffers.
+   Disable dropout and sampling. Allocate separate scratch for exactly three query tokens. The physical cache
+   indices and rotary positions of those tokens are P, P+1, P+2. Queries may attend to all Π and their own causal
+   prefix of the three-token block, never the external stack or an earlier step's scratch. Reuse buffers only
+   when the runtime guarantees the immutable Π prefix is not overwritten.
+5. **Implement the same three-token step.** Feed `[top_id, state_id, event_id]` as one block over Π. Use the
+   full-vocabulary argmax at the event position as the next state. Apply the host operation for the *incoming*
+   `(q, top, event)` row; do not replace the model's output with the reference target. Discard all three scratch
+   slots. Do not split the top token into a one-token prefill: that is a different numerical path. The step's
+   frame KV is scratch slot P across every layer, and the stack stores symbols, never those vectors.
+6. **Certify on the actual browser device.** Evaluate all 50/144/294 rows with the same batch size, shapes,
+   precision, mask and cache path as deployment. Require every full-vocabulary winner to equal its target with
+   strictly positive winner–runner-up margin. Retain logits per row and a slot-P frame per symbol; compare frames
+   across all rows sharing that symbol. A desktop H100/L4 certificate cannot authorize a browser export. Stop
+   on any failure; do not silently use a host lookup of the target state.
+7. **Run the port acceptance suite.** Replay the registered cells (depths 8/64/512/4,096 and L20000), all 72 random
+   instances, malformed inputs and BBH 250. Check each state against the reference and each full logit vector
+   and frame against the browser certificate, as `run_canonical` does. Hash Π before/after runs to catch cache
+   mutation. Repeat after changing depth/history and input order. If bitwise equality fails, report the observed
+   deviations and recertify the actual path; do not turn a sampled maximum into a universal bound.
+8. **Measure and retain provenance.** Run inference in a Web Worker, keep Π on the GPU, and yield progress between
+   short chunks of steps. Measure synchronized wall milliseconds per step and peak device memory separately
+   with and without auditing overhead. Log artifact hashes, certificate margins, device/runtime versions and
+   input hashes. Re-certify after any configuration change. Attention cache size is fixed by P+3; host stack
+   storage grows with nesting depth. The Python prototype copies the host stack on updates; a browser array
+   can push/pop in place while preserving the same semantics.
+
+## Reproduction and provenance
+
+- `manifests/probe.json` and `manifests/counted.json` bind the original code hashes and job arguments. The latter
+  refers to commit `61e6f44`; its four recorded call IDs were resumed by collection, not relaunched at takeover.
+- `manifests/l4.json` records the later L4 deployment's hashes. The H100 and L4 executor sources are identical;
+  the later source bundle additionally includes the offline report and validation scripts.
+- Run `nice -n 19 python3 -m unittest discover -s research/stack -p test_stack_machine.py -v`,
+  `nice -n 19 python3 research/stack/stack_validate.py --out research/stack/results/validation.json`, then
+  `nice -n 19 python3 research/stack/stack_report.py` to reproduce the local checks and Results section.
+- Remote protocol is deploy → plan → spawn → collect. Use the recorded manifests and ledger; do not re-spawn
+  completed/running IDs. `collect` uses `FunctionCall.get(timeout=0)`, returns immediately for running calls,
+  and settles completed calls. Long deployment commands are detached with logs; no foreground server is needed.
+- The ledger reserves GPU + maximum CPU/RAM rates plus startup before launch, caps total commitments at $20,
+  and settles from recorded wall time. The final report lists all jobs, including failures if any.
