+**Certified rows.** These are all rows witnessed by a concrete stack. Stability between stack limits 6 and 10 is
+only a diagnostic, not a completeness proof. `stack_validate.closed_cover` independently checks an inductive upper
+bound: Dyck permits OK/BAD/HR with any frame and HA only with BOT; Boolean permits Z/T/F/E/HE with any frame and
+HT/HF only with BOT. Initialization is in the set. For each pair and event, the check considers every possible
+parent exposed by a pop and verifies that the successor pair stays in the set and BOT is preserved. Deeper
+ancestors cannot affect this transition. Every pair in this closed upper bound also has a concrete witness from
+the search, so the witnessed rows are complete at arbitrary depth. The offline audit checks 110, 576 and 2,009
+pair/event/parent cases respectively, without changing the tables used by the recorded GPU jobs.
 
