+If any step is not bitwise equal, the fallback diagnostic is the margin rule: every row's margin must exceed
+2·max |Δlogit|. A maximum measured across sampled steps certifies only those perturbations; an all-execution
+robustness claim needs a uniform bound. The unbounded-depth argument instead uses the fixed-view invariant and
+assumes deterministic inference on the certified path.
+
+The call/return partition fixes stack height changes before a halt, except returns at BOT. Boolean internal
+events may rewrite the top symbol, and a call may store a left operand in the parent before pushing. Thus this
+is a visibly driven pushdown interpreter with top rewrites, rather than the strict textbook VPA syntax in which
+internal transitions leave the stack untouched. Halted machines freeze on all symbols. These conventions are
+part of the host semantics and the certificate, including malformed inputs.
 
